d's largest nocturnal primate.","revisionId":1375553473,"title":"Aye-aye","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aye-aye","wikidataId":"Q186778"}},{"commonNames":[{"language":"en","name":"Procellaria Petrels","source":"Catalogue of Life"},{"language":"en","name":"petrel","source":"The Paleobiology Database"}],"gbif":{"canonicalName":"Procellaria","confidence":92,"rank":"genus","scientificName":"Procellaria Linnaeus, 1758","status":"ACCEPTED","usageKey":2481430},"ottId":85287,"rank":"genus","scientificName":"Procellaria","synonyms":["Adamastor","Porcellaria"],"wikipedia":{"extract":"Procellaria is a genus of Southern Ocean long-winged seabirds related to prions, and the type genus of the order Procellariiformes. The black petrel (Procellaria parkinsoni) ranges in the Pacific Ocean, and as far north as Central America.","revisionId":1354731135,"title":"Procellaria","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Procellaria","wikidataId":"Q636683"}},{"commonNames":[{"language":"en","name":"Laotian Langur","source":"The IUCN Red List of Threatened Species"},{"language":"en","name":"Laotian","source":"Catalogue of Life"},{"language":"en","name":"Lao Langur","source":"Catalogue of Life"},{"language":"en","name":"Laos Langur","source":"Catalogue of Life"},{"language":"en","name":"Laotian Lutung","source":"Catalogue of Life"},{"language":"en","name":"Lao leaf monkey","source":"Catalogue of Life"}],"gbif":{"canonicalName":"Trachypithecus laotum","confidence":99,"rank":"species","scientificName":"Trachypithecus laotum (Thomas, 1921)","status":"ACCEPTED","usageKey":4267078},"ottId":250663,"rank":"species","scientificName":"Trachypithecus laotum","synonyms":["Pithecus laotum"],"wikipedia":{"extract":"The Laotian langur or white-browed black langur (Trachypithecus laotum) is a species of the primate family Cercopithecidae that is endemic to Laos in Southeast Asia. It is closely related to other primates found in the region such as Indochinese black langur and Hatinh langur.","revisionId":13